{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Adam knew, etc.</b> Lamech came to Adam the first man and lodged a complaint about his wives. He said to them: 'Is it for you to scrutinize the decree of the Omnipresent? Do your commandments, and He will do what is His.' They said to him: 'Straighten yourself first! Did you not separate from your wife these hundred and thirty years, ever since death was incurred through you?' Immediately, 'And Adam knew, etc.' And what is 'again'? To teach that desire was added upon his desire (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:35.036236648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}